  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting the Sumatran Elephant Population in Beutong Region, The Leuser Ecosystem, Aceh Province, Indonesia.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This award supports a comprehensive program to protect the Critically Endangered Sumatran elephant in the Beutong region in the northwest Leuser ecosystem, Aceh, Sumatra, Indonesia, by significantly reducing human-elephant conflict (HEC), monitoring wild elephant populations, anti-poaching patrols, and community outreach. Project activities include: 1) recruit and train two wildlife project teams, with each team including a forest police officer; 2) equip teams with rations, fuel, and basic patrol gear such as tents, GPS units, cameras, and uniforms; 3) mobilization of patrol teams with each team patrolling for a minimum of 15 days per month; 4) reporting all wildlife crimes and violations to District police; and 5) regular SMART patrol data entry and report synthesis with SMART reports submitted to the Aceh government and forest authorities. This project is an important first step in protecting the Beuton subpopulation of Sumatran elephants by reducing poaching and electrocution and poisoning deaths of elephants, and increased community awareness of elephant conservation issues in the Leuser ecosystem of Aceh, Indonesia.</narrative>
  </description>
